    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §3, Chap 435 of 2014",
    "lawSection": "Environmental Conservation",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S5511\n\n TITLE OF BILL :  An act to amend chapter 435 of the laws of 2014\namending the environmental conservation law relating to defining\nspearguns and allowing recreational spearfishing in New York's marine\nand coastal waters, in relation to extending the effectiveness thereof\n\n PURPOSE :\n\nTo extend the provisions of Chapter 435 of the Laws of 2014, which\nallows for recreational spearfishing in New York's marine and coastal\nwaters, for three years.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nExtends for three years the provisions of Section 3 of Chapter 435 of\nthe Laws of 2014 amending the Environmental Conservation Law relating\nto defining spearguns and allowing recreational spearfishing in New\nYork's marine and coastal waters\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nThe current law which allows for recreational spearfishing in New\nYork's marine and coastal waters sunsets on June 1, 2017. This\nlegislation is necessary to extend the effectiveness of this law for\nan additional three years to June 1, 2020.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\n2017: New Legislation\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nNone.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
